# Local dependencies and generated output are not release source.
node_modules/
/.next/
/dist/
/dist-vps/
/dist-contributor/
/coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Disposable PostgreSQL data directories created by test lanes. Must stay
# inside the worktree: `with-test-slot` only stops postmasters whose -D data
# directory is under its $PWD, so a cluster in the system temp dir is invisible
# to it. (scripts/dev/cleanup-test-postgres.mjs does NOT see these either — it
# only treats a directory as disposable when it is under os.tmpdir() or carries
# a mac-local-rehearsal marker, neither of which a test lane writes. The
# in-process teardown in tests/helpers/disposable-postgres-cluster.ts is what
# actually stops them.)
/.test-tmp/

# Local credentials and environment overrides. Examples must contain placeholders.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
*.pem
*.key

# Local execution logs and operating-system metadata.
*.log
*.ndjson
.DS_Store

# Job reports live outside the repo.
/reports/

# Playwright scratch output from a local owner-journey run: traces, screencasts
# and per-test artifacts. Nothing here belongs in the repository, and it is large
# enough that committing it by accident is a nuisance. CI writes its own copy to
# this same path and uploads it as an artifact, which is unaffected.
#
# Each producer is named rather than ignoring `test-results/` wholesale, so a
# source directory that happens to be called test-results is not silently
# ignored, and so a third scratch producer has to be added deliberately instead
# of inheriting this rule:
#   playwright.config.ts                 -> /test-results/playwright
#   scripts/owner-page-screenshots.mjs    -> /test-results/owner-screenshots
/test-results/playwright/
/test-results/owner-screenshots/

# Do not add automation without an explicit budget/security review.
# The CI workflow is reviewed in docs/ci-budget-security-review.md. Anything
# further needs its own review; this line no longer blocks the directory, so the
# rule above is the guard.
